# What `bun run deploy:backend` leaves out of the upload. The image installs and generates for
# itself, so dependencies and generated code stay behind, along with whatever only the web app,
# the design system or a local machine needs.
#
# Everything git ignores is left out first, which is what keeps a checkout's dotenv files, the
# Gemini key in `packages/strategydance-translations/.env` among them, out of the build context
# and the image. The lines after it are what git keeps but the image does not need
#!include:.gitignore

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.husky/
.claude/
.agents/
.firebase/
.DS_Store

# The credentials file google-github-actions/auth writes into the workspace when the deploy
# workflow runs. It would otherwise be uploaded, and `COPY . .` would bake it into the image
gha-creds-*.json

node_modules/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

emulators-data/
firebase-export-*/
temp-do-not-commit-or-delete/

packages/strategydance-database/generated/
packages/strategydance-database/.dataconnect/
packages/strategydance-web/dist/
packages/strategydance-design-system/storybook-static/
